# MetalFX Temporal and Frame Generation are always on, with no rows (dm_video.c load_once, nvn_mv.inc, nvn_fg.inc): the game starts with both on this Mac's Recommended. The Video tab has no row for them, for anti-aliasing or for the
# frame rate, so ten DOWN presses go from Display Mode to Frame Drops, the last row (a video_row event naming another row means the rows changed), where RIGHT goes from this Mac's Lower (rays are on, dm_picrec.c) to Keep. A 3D Resolution of 75% rebuilds the scaler and the interpolator live,
# and 100% again. Performance leaves them alone (video_presets_mac.scn). Rows: mode, res, color, preset, s3d, aniso, envsh, shq, envd, rt, drops
name video_fg_mac
requires mac-app
save warlock
env DM_TEST_VIDEO_FIRSTBOOT=1
timeout 240

enter_game
sleep 5
open_pause
tap_ui Settings
sleep 2
inputmode mode=controller
sleep 1
press DOWN
press DOWN
press DOWN
press DOWN
press DOWN
press DOWN
press DOWN
press DOWN
press DOWN
press DOWN
press RIGHT
sleep 1
screenshot video_rows.png
msg OptionsPanelMessage:AcceptChanges
sleep 3
press UP
press UP
press UP
press UP
press UP
press UP
press RIGHT
sleep 0.5
press RIGHT
sleep 1
msg OptionsPanelMessage:AcceptChanges
sleep 5
screenshot fg_75.png
press LEFT
sleep 0.5
press LEFT
sleep 1
msg OptionsPanelMessage:AcceptChanges
sleep 5
quit
check event picture how=first up=2 fg=1
check event video_row row=drops value=1
check event video_row row=s3d
check event picture how=apply up=2 fg=1
check event scale3d pct=75
check event scale3d pct=99
check log_has "temporal scaler: .* built in" min=3
check log_has "temporal scaler: camera jitter seen"
check log_has "frame generation: interpolator .* built in" min=3
check no_red
check no_red_log
